1
00:01:28,098 --> 00:01:33,970
RUN, HONDA! FOR YOUR LOVE!

2
00:01:42,045 --> 00:01:43,180
Outta the way!

3
00:01:43,413 --> 00:01:44,981
This ain't no Sunday drive!

4
00:01:52,956 --> 00:01:55,959
Hey, Nakagawa. You getting hungry?

5
00:01:56,159 --> 00:01:58,929
I'm feeling stir-fry with dumplings for lunch.

6
00:01:59,129 --> 00:02:00,730
Chinese food? Sounds good.

7
00:02:12,776 --> 00:02:14,544
Honda! You almost hit me!

8
00:02:14,945 --> 00:02:17,314
Calm down, Ryotsu, my man.

9
00:02:19,015 --> 00:02:22,452
More importantly, I'm buying lunch. Want me to get you anything?

10
00:02:22,652 --> 00:02:23,954
No, we're ordering out.

11
00:02:24,621 --> 00:02:26,456
My treat?

12
00:02:28,558 --> 00:02:31,962
Honda-kun, why didn't you say so?

13
00:02:32,796 --> 00:02:34,831
I'll have the luxe pork cutlet set.

14
00:02:35,031 --> 00:02:37,667
Pork miso soup too. Haven't had that in a while.

15
00:02:37,868 --> 00:02:40,203
Man, you really are a freeloader.

16
00:02:40,403 --> 00:02:41,204
Nakagawa?

17
00:02:41,638 --> 00:02:43,206
You're buying for me too?

18
00:02:43,406 --> 00:02:44,241
Sure, why not?

19
00:02:44,474 --> 00:02:47,511
It's his treat, so don't go ordering anything expensive.

20
00:02:47,711 --> 00:02:49,546
Maybe the fried chicken set?

21
00:02:49,779 --> 00:02:50,814
Got it.

22
00:02:55,051 --> 00:02:59,156
Okay then. Ryotsu, Nakagawa. I'll be back soon!

23
00:03:00,557 --> 00:03:03,360
Not many people have such 180-degree personalities.

24
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,528
Yeah.

25
00:03:05,662 --> 00:03:07,564
Thank you very much.

26
00:03:11,334 --> 00:03:12,269
H-Hello.

27
00:03:13,203 --> 00:03:14,437
Oh, hello.

28
00:03:14,671 --> 00:03:16,039
Box lunch again today?

29
00:03:16,239 --> 00:03:20,043
Yes. You always make the best box lunches.

30
00:03:20,243 --> 00:03:21,511
I'm happy to hear that.

31
00:03:21,711 --> 00:03:23,280
What would you like today?

32
00:03:23,613 --> 00:03:27,551
Um, can I get a luxe pork cutlet set, and a fried chicken set.

33
00:03:27,751 --> 00:03:29,186
-And also a seaweed— -Box lunch ready!

34
00:03:29,386 --> 00:03:31,254
-And two— -Thank you!

35
00:03:31,988 --> 00:03:37,260
So that's two luxe pork cutlet sets, two fried chicken sets, and two seaweed sets?

36
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,863
-Huh? -Is that wrong?

37
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:45,869
No, that's fine. And pork miso soup too.

38
00:03:46,236 --> 00:03:48,104
So six bowls of pork miso soup.

39
00:03:48,305 --> 00:03:50,106
Oh, uh, yes...

40
00:03:50,307 --> 00:03:54,377
Two luxe porks, two fried chickens, two seaweeds, and six pork soups please!

41
00:03:54,578 --> 00:03:56,112
Coming up!

42
00:03:56,713 --> 00:03:58,782
Here you are. Two box lunches.

43
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:09,593
Thanks for buying our lunches as well.

44
00:04:09,793 --> 00:04:12,028
My pleasure. You're always helping me out.

45
00:04:12,229 --> 00:04:14,631
Now that's the right kind of attitude.

46
00:04:15,232 --> 00:04:17,667
Not like some others around here.

47
00:04:17,901 --> 00:04:20,637
Hey, somebody. Chief's talking to you.

48
00:04:20,871 --> 00:04:22,339
I'm talking about you!

49
00:04:24,441 --> 00:04:26,743
The rice is a bit dry, don't you think?

50
00:04:26,943 --> 00:04:28,144
Yes, you're right.

51
00:04:28,345 --> 00:04:33,216
No, it can't be dry. They use only the best Koshihikari rice.

52
00:04:34,618 --> 00:04:36,419
The pickles are kinda salty too.

53
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,655
They're just the right level of salty.

54
00:04:39,222 --> 00:04:40,991
Their box lunches are perfect.

55
00:04:41,224 --> 00:04:43,593
They're made with passion and love.

56
00:04:43,793 --> 00:04:45,161
-Oh, I get it. -Huh?

57
00:04:45,362 --> 00:04:48,164
You ordered too many lunches on purpose

58
00:04:48,365 --> 00:04:51,668
because they're paying you to advertise them, right?

59
00:04:51,902 --> 00:04:53,370
No, they're not.

60
00:04:53,837 --> 00:04:54,638
I got it.

61
00:04:55,305 --> 00:04:59,676
Honda-san. I'll bet you like the girl who works there, don't you?

62
00:05:02,245 --> 00:05:04,114
No, not really...

63
00:05:04,314 --> 00:05:07,350
So that's it. She is very cute.

64
00:05:07,951 --> 00:05:10,020
How did you know?

65
00:05:10,253 --> 00:05:13,189
Your face as red as a traffic light gives it away.

66
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:14,524
Oh dear...

67
00:05:14,858 --> 00:05:17,294
So, does the girl have a name?

68
00:05:18,495 --> 00:05:20,997
Her name's Megumi Hoshino.

69
00:05:21,331 --> 00:05:24,668
Honda, I say this out of love, but this is a lost cause.

70
00:05:24,868 --> 00:05:27,203
Huh? Why would you say that?

71
00:05:27,404 --> 00:05:29,673
Ryo-chan. I thought you two were friends?

72
00:05:29,873 --> 00:05:31,374
You should help him out.

73
00:05:31,708 --> 00:05:36,880
Reiko, do you know how many times this guy's had his heart broken?

74
00:05:37,113 --> 00:05:39,649
Not just once or twice. At least a hundred times!

75
00:05:39,849 --> 00:05:42,752
-To be precise, it's 101 times. -That many?

76
00:05:42,986 --> 00:05:46,890
And every time it happens, I have to help him drown his sorrows.

77
00:05:47,123 --> 00:05:49,893
-But... -Don't bother, Reiko.

78
00:05:50,126 --> 00:05:55,298
Ryotsu was born romantically challenged. He could never act as Cupid anyway.

79
00:05:57,033 --> 00:05:59,536
Now that I can't unhear!

80
00:06:00,537 --> 00:06:01,604
Chief!

81
00:06:01,838 --> 00:06:02,772
What?

82
00:06:03,006 --> 00:06:08,044
You insult my reputation as a salt-and-pepper ladies' man.

83
00:06:08,511 --> 00:06:10,914
A salt-and-pepper ladies' man? You?

84
00:06:11,147 --> 00:06:13,049
That's funnier than your monobrow.

85
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:14,718
Damn it...

86
00:06:14,918 --> 00:06:19,389
I'll show you! I'll do whatever it takes to make that girl and Honda an item.

87
00:06:19,589 --> 00:06:20,757
You'd do that for me?

88
00:06:21,358 --> 00:06:24,260
Sure, leave it to me. It'll all be plain flailing.

89
00:06:24,461 --> 00:06:26,029
You mean "plain sailing."

90
00:06:27,063 --> 00:06:30,266
Anyway, I'll definitely get you a date with Megumi-chan.

91
00:06:30,934 --> 00:06:32,569
Thank you so much, Ryotsu.

92
00:06:33,002 --> 00:06:34,204
Sure thing!

93
00:06:58,661 --> 00:07:00,797
Well? How did it go?

94
00:07:01,364 --> 00:07:03,800
No good. She likes another guy.

95
00:07:06,503 --> 00:07:07,303
No way...

96
00:07:12,742 --> 00:07:15,812
Did she say what he's like?

97
00:07:16,513 --> 00:07:20,950
She's got a crush on some motorcycle cop who rides by at nine o'clock each morning.

98
00:07:21,151 --> 00:07:24,587
Sorry, man, but you'd best give up on her.

99
00:07:25,121 --> 00:07:28,958
But I'm a motorcycle cop too.

100
00:07:30,527 --> 00:07:34,431
And I also ride by at nine o'clock each morning.

101
00:07:36,232 --> 00:07:37,867
What did you say?

102
00:07:39,636 --> 00:07:42,272
I said I ride by at nine o'clock each morning.

103
00:07:42,472 --> 00:07:43,173
Oh!

104
00:07:44,007 --> 00:07:45,809
Come with me, Honda!

105
00:07:47,944 --> 00:07:49,679
-Excuse me... -Yes?

106
00:07:49,879 --> 00:07:53,616
The motorcycle cop you mentioned. It's this guy, right?

107
00:07:53,817 --> 00:07:54,784
Look.

108
00:07:55,718 --> 00:07:57,420
Oh, you're one of our regulars.

109
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,422
H-Hello there...

110
00:07:59,956 --> 00:08:01,091
Well? Same guy?

111
00:08:01,291 --> 00:08:04,894
Huh? No, he looks nothing like him.

112
00:08:07,363 --> 00:08:09,466
Oh, I'm sorry.

113
00:08:09,866 --> 00:08:13,870
You're both quite slim, but the other guy has a more chiseled face.

114
00:08:14,337 --> 00:08:17,173
He rolls his sleeves up, and lets his scarf flutter.

115
00:08:17,373 --> 00:08:19,876
He's so manly and cool!

116
00:08:20,844 --> 00:08:22,846
That really is me...

117
00:08:23,046 --> 00:08:25,715
-Take a closer look. -Ryotsu!

118
00:08:28,852 --> 00:08:30,920
No, his face is too different.

119
00:08:31,154 --> 00:08:34,457
It may be hard to believe, but when this guy gets on his bike,

120
00:08:34,657 --> 00:08:37,927
his face and his personality do a complete 180.

121
00:08:38,294 --> 00:08:39,696
So your name is Honda?

122
00:08:40,163 --> 00:08:44,701
Honda's the best motorcycle cop we've got.

123
00:08:45,168 --> 00:08:46,769
Oh, that's perfect!

124
00:08:47,003 --> 00:08:52,942
You must know who rides past here each morning if you're both on motorcycles.

125
00:08:53,176 --> 00:08:54,577
No, that's not what I—

126
00:08:54,777 --> 00:08:58,047
Yes, I'll find out. I promise.

127
00:08:58,915 --> 00:09:02,919
Great! Please let me know as soon as you find out.

128
00:09:03,353 --> 00:09:04,420
I will.

129
00:09:07,857 --> 00:09:10,260
Why would you make such a silly promise?

130
00:09:10,493 --> 00:09:11,561
I'm sorry...

131
00:09:11,761 --> 00:09:13,963
Well, this is getting complicated.

132
00:09:14,197 --> 00:09:17,200
So Megumi-san prefers Honda-san on his bike,

133
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:19,769
but not as he is right now?

134
00:09:22,405 --> 00:09:24,774
Honda. There's only one way forward now.

135
00:09:25,175 --> 00:09:26,776
What should I do?

136
00:09:27,110 --> 00:09:31,047
You just have to stay on your motorcycle anytime you're around Megumi-chan.

137
00:09:31,247 --> 00:09:32,549
-Huh? -What?

138
00:09:32,749 --> 00:09:34,050
That's impossible.

139
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:35,718
I know it is.

140
00:09:35,919 --> 00:09:40,290
But ask her out while on your motorcycle and she's bound to agree.

141
00:09:40,523 --> 00:09:43,760
-But even if she does... -It feels a bit pushy.

142
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,262
How you start a relationship is crucial.

143
00:09:46,462 --> 00:09:50,366
Get the start right, and everything else will fall into place.

144
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,302
Is that how it works?

145
00:09:52,802 --> 00:09:56,639
This salt-and-pepper ladies' man is never wrong.

146
00:09:58,775 --> 00:09:59,576
I'll do it!

147
00:09:59,776 --> 00:10:00,743
Honda-san!

148
00:10:00,944 --> 00:10:03,146
I really like her.

149
00:10:03,379 --> 00:10:07,317
As long as I get to go on a date with her, I don't care how it ends up.

150
00:10:07,984 --> 00:10:11,220
Okay, enough talk. Now we figure out your plan of attack.

151
00:10:11,421 --> 00:10:12,989
Yes, sir!

152
00:10:22,932 --> 00:10:24,834
Oh, good morning.

153
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:29,772
Did Honda-san tell you about me?

154
00:10:29,973 --> 00:10:30,974
Uh, yeah.

155
00:10:31,407 --> 00:10:36,246
Oh, I should introduce myself. I'm Megumi Hoshino.

156
00:10:36,446 --> 00:10:37,680
What's your name?

157
00:10:38,481 --> 00:10:39,349
I'm Honda.

158
00:10:39,582 --> 00:10:41,618
Your name is also Honda?

159
00:10:41,818 --> 00:10:45,121
Uh, no, I'm Honda's buddy. My name's Suzuki.

160
00:10:45,488 --> 00:10:47,056
So your name is Suzuki?

161
00:10:47,490 --> 00:10:49,993
I don't normally let gals ride my motorcycle.

162
00:10:50,193 --> 00:10:54,030
But if you're willing to trust me, I'll give you the ride of a lifetime.

163
00:10:57,467 --> 00:10:59,535
Yes, I'd love to.

164
00:10:59,869 --> 00:11:02,839
All right. I'll stop by at nine on Sunday to pick you up.

165
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:04,040
Okay.

166
00:11:04,474 --> 00:11:05,375
See you.

167
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:16,719
This'll definitely get me the prize money.

168
00:11:20,189 --> 00:11:21,524
Ryotsu, my man.

169
00:11:22,492 --> 00:11:24,761
I did it! We're going on a date this Sunday.

170
00:11:25,194 --> 00:11:26,996
That's great. Well done!

171
00:11:27,196 --> 00:11:31,167
Now listen. You have to stay on your motorcycle for the entire date, okay?

172
00:11:31,734 --> 00:11:32,735
Okay.

173
00:11:45,114 --> 00:11:46,549
Suzuki-san.

174
00:11:47,717 --> 00:11:49,052
Suzuki-san!

175
00:11:49,252 --> 00:11:50,586
Yeah?

176
00:11:50,787 --> 00:11:54,590
I never knew the wind could feel so nice.

177
00:11:54,791 --> 00:11:57,560
Yeah? I'm glad you like it.

178
00:11:58,861 --> 00:12:00,963
I'm Suzuki, remember?

179
00:12:08,438 --> 00:12:10,673
Hey, lovebirds! Where you going?

180
00:12:15,878 --> 00:12:18,948
This ain't no place for a romantic Sunday drive!

181
00:12:20,149 --> 00:12:22,952
You wanna say that again, buddy?

182
00:12:23,353 --> 00:12:24,620
Yikes! Honda-san!

183
00:12:26,522 --> 00:12:28,791
I'm not Honda. I'm his buddy, Suzuki!

184
00:12:32,829 --> 00:12:34,764
So sorry about that.

185
00:12:34,964 --> 00:12:37,967
I never would have done it knowing it was you, Honda-san.

186
00:12:38,367 --> 00:12:39,736
I'm Suzuki, you idiot!

187
00:12:39,936 --> 00:12:41,571
Sorry, Suzuki-san!

188
00:12:41,771 --> 00:12:43,539
We're sorry, Suzuki-san!

189
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:45,274
All right.

190
00:12:45,475 --> 00:12:47,777
I'll let you off the hook this time.

191
00:12:47,977 --> 00:12:50,546
But do that again, and you'll regret it!

192
00:12:50,747 --> 00:12:51,647
Yes, sir!

193
00:12:52,415 --> 00:12:53,182
Are you okay?

194
00:12:53,416 --> 00:12:57,653
Yes. I don't need to be scared so long as I have you around.

195
00:12:58,187 --> 00:13:00,656
All right, hold on tight.

196
00:13:00,857 --> 00:13:01,824
Okay!

197
00:13:09,565 --> 00:13:14,003
That's strange. I could have sworn that was Honda-san.

198
00:13:33,022 --> 00:13:36,526
You're really manly and strong.

199
00:13:36,993 --> 00:13:38,528
I love it!

200
00:13:40,797 --> 00:13:42,532
-Wanna catch a movie? -Sure!

201
00:13:51,474 --> 00:13:52,875
There's empty seats...

202
00:13:53,342 --> 00:13:55,878
This is how I watch movies. Don't worry about it.

203
00:13:57,013 --> 00:13:58,381
You sure are different.

204
00:14:46,262 --> 00:14:49,765
You really love your motorcycle, don't you?

205
00:14:49,966 --> 00:14:52,935
Yeah, it's the perfect partner.

206
00:14:53,302 --> 00:14:55,605
My bike is like an extension of my soul.

207
00:14:58,975 --> 00:15:01,310
The perfect partner, huh?

208
00:15:09,585 --> 00:15:10,853
What's wrong?

209
00:15:11,854 --> 00:15:16,125
To tell you the truth, my ex is leaving for America today.

210
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,594
Oh, you have a boyfriend?

211
00:15:20,296 --> 00:15:21,597
Transferred to America?

212
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:28,471
Megumi-san, would you come...

213
00:15:28,704 --> 00:15:29,538
Huh?

214
00:15:29,906 --> 00:15:32,708
No, it's nothing.

215
00:15:33,309 --> 00:15:35,978
Two years will fly by. We'll be together again soon.

216
00:15:39,348 --> 00:15:40,550
Is that all?

217
00:15:42,118 --> 00:15:44,654
Go to America. Or wherever. See if I care!

218
00:15:45,421 --> 00:15:46,355
Goodbye!

219
00:15:46,756 --> 00:15:48,457
Megumi-san!

220
00:15:53,629 --> 00:15:55,298
But it's okay.

221
00:15:56,432 --> 00:15:57,600
It's over.

222
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,970
I don't want to date someone as wishy-washy as him.

223
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:07,476
Guys should be manly like you, Suzuki-san.

224
00:16:08,577 --> 00:16:10,446
You think?

225
00:16:12,148 --> 00:16:12,982
We should go.

226
00:16:13,849 --> 00:16:14,817
Okay.

227
00:16:17,787 --> 00:16:18,587
Excuse me...

228
00:16:18,788 --> 00:16:20,356
Hello there.

229
00:16:26,495 --> 00:16:27,630
What's up?

230
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,966
Wait here for a moment, okay?

231
00:16:35,972 --> 00:16:37,039
All right, finished.

232
00:16:37,239 --> 00:16:39,375
I can't hold it anymore!

233
00:16:41,377 --> 00:16:44,146
Hey, how'd the date go?

234
00:16:44,513 --> 00:16:49,085
You were right. I stayed on the motorcycle and it's all going perfectly.

235
00:16:49,318 --> 00:16:51,087
Really? Good job, you stud!

236
00:17:02,631 --> 00:17:03,432
Oh!

237
00:17:09,672 --> 00:17:10,439
Megumi-san.

238
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:13,075
Yamamoto-san!

239
00:17:14,844 --> 00:17:17,546
Come on, Ryotsu. You'll ruin my groove.

240
00:17:17,747 --> 00:17:21,050
Hey, remember who got you this date in the first place?

241
00:17:28,257 --> 00:17:30,226
Who's that guy?

242
00:17:31,894 --> 00:17:36,732
To tell you the truth, my ex is leaving for America today.

243
00:17:40,202 --> 00:17:43,906
What's going on, Honda? Who is he?

244
00:17:45,941 --> 00:17:47,209
Hey, you mutt!

245
00:17:48,577 --> 00:17:51,881
I must tell you something before I leave.

246
00:17:52,314 --> 00:17:53,115
Huh?

247
00:17:54,617 --> 00:17:58,888
Megumi-san, I love you. I want us to get married.

248
00:18:02,491 --> 00:18:04,460
This is a plane ticket in your name.

249
00:18:04,693 --> 00:18:06,595
I'd like you to come with me.

250
00:18:09,165 --> 00:18:10,332
What, all of a sudden?

251
00:18:10,566 --> 00:18:13,769
You're right... You can't just drop everything on a whim.

252
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:16,872
I always screw up like this.

253
00:18:19,175 --> 00:18:20,342
Well, take care.

254
00:18:38,327 --> 00:18:39,662
That took a while.

255
00:18:39,895 --> 00:18:41,530
-Do you have a passport? -Huh?

256
00:18:41,764 --> 00:18:43,499
I asked if you have a passport.

257
00:18:43,733 --> 00:18:45,367
Yes, but...

258
00:18:46,802 --> 00:18:51,440
We'll stop by your place, then we're heading for the airport.

259
00:18:52,908 --> 00:18:55,311
Damn it! You stupid dog!

260
00:18:55,511 --> 00:18:57,346
Next time, I'm gonna arrest you!

261
00:18:58,814 --> 00:19:00,182
Hey, Honda!

262
00:19:00,683 --> 00:19:02,818
What's gotten into him?

263
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:07,223
You like this Yamamoto guy, right?

264
00:19:10,626 --> 00:19:13,028
Being manly ain't just about looks.

265
00:19:13,229 --> 00:19:17,800
A real man is committed to the woman he loves.

266
00:19:18,567 --> 00:19:20,102
Suzuki-san...

267
00:19:25,674 --> 00:19:28,477
Damn this traffic.

268
00:19:31,814 --> 00:19:34,250
What time is the flight?

269
00:19:34,483 --> 00:19:35,651
Seven o'clock.

270
00:19:38,387 --> 00:19:41,423
Damn. We won't make it at this rate.

271
00:19:42,858 --> 00:19:44,894
-Hold on tight. -Huh?

272
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:13,222
"NEW TOKYO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT"

273
00:20:13,989 --> 00:20:15,157
Thank you all so much.

274
00:20:15,357 --> 00:20:17,560
C'mon, don't look so glum.

275
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,764
A transfer to Los Angeles means you're on the fast track for promotion.

276
00:20:23,766 --> 00:20:25,768
"NARITA EXIT 1 KM"

277
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:29,638
Okay, I'd better go.

278
00:20:29,872 --> 00:20:31,874
-Good luck. -Yeah.

279
00:20:38,047 --> 00:20:40,449
-Take care! -Remember to call once in a while.

280
00:20:40,649 --> 00:20:42,017
Good luck!

281
00:21:02,238 --> 00:21:03,906
Megumi-san?

282
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,348
Go on.

283
00:21:24,126 --> 00:21:26,328
I... I've decided...

284
00:21:27,162 --> 00:21:29,531
I've decided to come with you.

285
00:21:30,232 --> 00:21:32,234
Please take me with you.

286
00:21:35,137 --> 00:21:36,472
Megumi-san...

287
00:21:37,907 --> 00:21:40,009
How long are you two gonna hug?

288
00:21:40,242 --> 00:21:42,177
Hurry up, or you'll miss your flight.

289
00:21:43,479 --> 00:21:45,981
Suzuki-san, how can I thank you enough?

290
00:21:46,382 --> 00:21:48,684
Don't worry about me. Go on.

291
00:21:48,917 --> 00:21:51,186
Okay. Thank you so much.

292
00:22:12,174 --> 00:22:14,310
Honda-san, it was you?

293
00:22:26,155 --> 00:22:38,200
Thank you, Honda-san!

294
00:22:41,036 --> 00:22:44,039
G-Goodbye, Megumi-san.

295
00:22:53,082 --> 00:22:55,184
She was such a nice girl...

296
00:22:55,384 --> 00:22:57,720
My 102nd heartbreak...

297
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,321
Come on, stop crying.

298
00:22:59,521 --> 00:23:02,591
And to top it off, my salary's been docked for six months.

299
00:23:02,791 --> 00:23:04,727
Well, that's a given.

300
00:23:05,794 --> 00:23:09,598
You know, Honda, to act as Cupid for the girl you love,

301
00:23:09,798 --> 00:23:12,768
man, you've gotta be a saint or an idiot.

302
00:23:13,001 --> 00:23:15,738
You're just like Ryo-san when he was young.

303
00:23:15,938 --> 00:23:20,709
Whenever he got his heart broken, he'd drown his sorrows here too.

304
00:23:20,909 --> 00:23:22,711
Hey, don't tell him that.

305
00:23:22,911 --> 00:23:24,613
No need to feel embarrassed.

306
00:23:24,813 --> 00:23:28,350
Oh, and Honda-san, 102 failed romances is nothing.

307
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:30,953
Ryo-san's had more than 300.

308
00:23:31,186 --> 00:23:33,022
Really?

309
00:23:33,222 --> 00:23:35,891
That kind of makes me feel better.

310
00:23:36,091 --> 00:23:38,460
Hey, Ryotsu. Let's get drunk!

311
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:43,799
If I get drunk, I'll get hungover, and then the chief will chew me out again.

312
00:23:44,033 --> 00:23:45,834
But aren't you always in trouble?

313
00:23:46,068 --> 00:23:49,104
What? Fine. But if we're gonna drink, we're going all out.

314
00:23:49,304 --> 00:23:51,240
I want these glasses licked clean!

315
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:53,475
Yes, sir!

316
00:23:54,076 --> 00:23:56,045
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

317
00:23:56,245 --> 00:24:01,950
TWO HANGOVERS, 18 DAMAGED CARS
